  "narrative": "All newly delivered comparisons are valid, with cell sizes above the minimum requirement. The six direct presence-context contrasts H105-H110 are extremely strong. For feature_037 in the claimed negative direction, signed estimates are +0.778 (H105, 95% interval +0.697 to +0.860) and +0.876 (H106, +0.781 to +0.972); for feature_010 in the claimed positive direction, signed estimates are +0.839 (H107, +0.758 to +0.920) and +0.870 (H108, +0.783 to +0.956); for feature_002 in the claimed positive direction, signed estimates are +0.722 (H109, +0.628 to +0.816) and +0.850 (H110, +0.765 to +0.936). Every lower signed bound is far above the 0.15-unit outcome threshold, so these are scientifically meaningful associations in the supplied dataset even with many prior comparisons. They support approximate separability of the three measured binary signals within this dataset: each remains large when exactly one other strong assay is positive. They are unadjusted conditional associations and not causal effects. The three lower-age triple-negative contrasts H111-H113 are likewise strong, with signed lower bounds of +0.784, +0.738, and +0.661, so the conditional associations are not confined to the older age stratum. The three feature_030-burden interaction contrasts H100-H102 are near null: signed point estimates are -0.008, -0.017, and +0.001, and every upper bound is below +0.15. I therefore reject them as evidence for meaningful feature_030 modification of the focal associations, while noting that a null does not prove absence of any interaction. I request validation of H107 specifically because feature_010's previously validated conditional anchor H74 was estimated only when feature_037 and feature_002 were negative; independent validation of the feature_010 contrast when feature_037 is positive directly tests whether feature_010 is independent of the opposite feature_037 signal.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 5 appraise update: The direct mixed co-assay contexts all show very large associations for feature_037, feature_010, and feature_002, with lower confidence bounds around 0.63 to 0.94 signed units. The lower-age triple-negative contexts also replicate all three associations. Together with validated H23, H74, and H75, this makes the three-assay pattern internally coherent and largely independent within the supplied dataset. The feature_030-burden interaction tests are null and closed. I requested validation of H107 to test feature_010 persistence in the presence of feature_037. Next analyze priorities: validate H107 result when delivered; consider newly proposed all-positive co-assay contexts, but treat cell-size failures as unresolved infeasible tests; if feasible, they would complete the 2x2x2 separability screen. Continue to treat all accepted claims as dataset-specific associations, not causal mechanisms or generalizable biology. Deferred exact numeric continuous contrasts and low-priority marker interactions should not crowd analysis budget unless a clear gap remains.",
